Z||000011||Fiero_24||08-30-2001||12:01 PM||||MD_Fiero.  Sorry, I have not checked this post in a while.  What you need to do is go into My computer, C:\, program files, then electronic arts, and go into cars (this is all in the C: drive).  There should be all the other car folders there as well.  From there you basically create a floder per car and add the download.  I have not tried it on the demo, but that is how I did it.  Let me know if it works.  I am not in front of my PC, so I am going on what I remember from when I did the install.<P><BR>Craig<P><BR>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
